  "answer": "Technical support answers must qualify the general statement that “PDF citations are available”: precise page- and paragraph-level citations depend heavily on document quality and are not guaranteed for image-only or low-quality scans [NL-002#NL-002-S09]. Scanned PDFs have no native text layer and require OCR; because OCR is heuristic, blurry or low-resolution scans can cause misread characters, broken layouts, missing citations, and incorrect page links [NL-006#NL-006-S03]. For these cases, agents should recommend checking scan quality and re-saving the document as a digital, text-searchable PDF or native DOCX/Markdown so citations map correctly [NL-028#NL-028-S03][NL-006#NL-006-S03]. If scanned files must be used, the Advanced OCR Pipeline should be recommended for better layout-aware extraction [NL-006#NL-006-S03].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
